<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30141" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mustĕus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		mustum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to new
			wine</i> or <i>must, like must.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mala, quae antea mustea vocabant, nunc melimela
					appellant,</span>”
				<i>must-apples</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 7, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mala,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 14, 15, § 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fructus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					9, 15, 13</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>young, new,
			fresh</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">musteus caseus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 42, 97, § 240</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">piper,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 7, 14, § 29</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">liber,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 8, 21, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
